    "alert_id": "ALERT_003",
    "title": "Missing VL monitoring plan for pregnancy",
    "message": "Guidelines require viral load monitoring 3 months after ART initiation in pregnancy, with repeat VL at delivery if gestation exceeds 28 weeks. Patient initiated ART 10 weeks ago and has a VL of 89 copies/mL today, which is appropriately suppressed. However, no clinician assessment or plan was documented today. A follow-up VL at approximately 6 months post-initiation and at delivery should be planned. The current VL result should be formally reviewed and documented.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Document VL review and plan repeat VL per pregnancy schedule: at delivery if >28 weeks gestation, and continue routine pregnancy VL monitoring.",
